  "hindi": "मैंने मद में आनन्दित होकर शम्बर के नौ के साथ नब्बे गढ़ों को बिखेर दिया; सौवें को, आवास को, सर्वथा, जब मैंने अतिथिग्व दिवोदास की सहायता की।",
  "english": "Exhilarated, I drove apart Śambara's strongholds, nine together with ninety; the hundredth, the dwelling, altogether, when I helped Divodāsa Atithigva.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "nava sākaṃ navatīḥ is rendered literally ('nine together with ninety'; the numeral phrase amounts to ninety-nine). The verb vy airam is not repeated for the second line: śatatamaṃ veśyam is taken as a further object of it, which is an assumption. veśyam and sarvatātā are uncertain (veśya 'dwelling' from viś; sarvatātā possibly a locative of sarvatāti 'completeness'). Atithigva is taken as a name or epithet of Divodāsa.",
  "confidence": "low"
