  "hindi": "वह पक्षी पक्षियों से आगे निकले, हे मरुतो; शीघ्र उड़ने वाला श्येन श्येनों से आगे निकले — जब सुन्दर पंखों वाले ने बिना चक्र की स्वधा से देवों को प्रिय हवि मनु के लिए वहन किया।",
  "english": "Let that bird surpass the birds, O Maruts; let the hawk, swift-flying, surpass the hawks, when the fair-winged one, by wheelless own power, bore the oblation favoured by the gods for Manu.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "pra ... astu is read as 'let (him) surpass' with the ablatives of comparison; this is an interpretation of a compressed construction. acakrayā svadhayā 'by wheelless own power' is literal; the form acakrayā could also be adverbial. su ṣa: ṣa is saḥ after su (sandhi spelling).",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
